<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm on plant demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm on plant demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Monday were firm in central Indian markets and were up by 200-300 rupees per tonne on good demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>Business volume was good and the undertone was strong.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also firm on limited supplies from processing plants and refineries. Prices were up by 300 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were slightly up on limited offerings from processors and exporters. Soymeal yellow was up by 300 rupees in local trading and up by $1 for export.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $249-250 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was down by 100 rupees and quoted at 3,125-3,150 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition and was $90-91 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export.</p>
